{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Hallelujah. I will give thanks to YHWH</b> — Hallelujah: the poet's words are 'praise YHWH, like me,' for I will give thanks to HaShem with all my heart." "<b>in the council of the upright</b> — in secret." "<b>and the congregation</b> — in public. And this is 'that I give thanks, saying.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 111, :notes {0 "Resolved ה' as HaShem per divine-name rules; the word הללויה is left untranslated as in the source."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:22.164980594Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}